{
  "name": "LDH kinetics: lactate oxidation by human LDH-A",
  "version": "2",
  "description": "L-lactate dehydrogenase A chain from Homo sapiens converts (S)-lactate to pyruvate. Formation of NADH followed photometrically at 340 nm; the decrease of (S)-lactate derived from it. Three starting concentrations spanning K_m (1, 5, 15 mM, K_m 4.4), 11 time points each over 20 min.\n\nSynthetic teaching dataset: the numbers come from a Michaelis-Menten simulation with added noise, not from a bench. The chemical and biological identifiers are real — the reaction from Rhea RHEA:23444, the enzyme from UniProt P00338.",
